  A trial newsletter, for checking that sending works before a real one
  goes out: `just newsletter-send app trial "" you@example.org`. It says
  what it is, so nobody who receives it by mistake is left wondering.

  A campaign extends newsletter.html.j2 and fills `subject`, `preheader`,
  `content` and `text`. Its name is this file's name, less the ending,
  and its brand is the folder it is in: `quill/` or `ldd/`.
-#}
{% extends "newsletter.html.j2" %}
{% import "_components.html.j2" as c with context %}
{% block subject %}A trial newsletter from Quill Medical{% endblock %}
{% block preheader %}Sent to check that newsletters, and unsubscribing from them, work.{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
{{ c.heading("A *trial* newsletter") }}
{{ c.paragraph("This is a test, sent to check that newsletters from Quill Medical arrive and look right. There is no news in it.") }}
{{ c.paragraph("If you were not expecting it, you can ignore it. The unsubscribe link below works, and so does the button your mailbox may show at the top.") }}
{% endblock %}

{% block text %}
A trial newsletter

This is a test, sent to check that newsletters from Quill Medical arrive and look right. There is no news in it.

If you were not expecting it, you can ignore it.

Unsubscribe: {{ unsubscribe_url }}

Mark Bailey, Bailey Medics
{% endblock %}
